        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 85-year-old male patient, admitted on 02/03/1996 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia. Blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. He was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout his stay. The patient responded well to treatment with improvement of symptoms and oxygenation. He was discharged on 03/03/1996 in stable condition. I recommend continuation of his inhaled maintenance therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
